---
id: org.dxos.plugin.uml
name: UmlPlugin
version: 0.1.0
---

UML for drawings: an assistant skill that draws class diagrams in any drawing, and a UML class shape for the
canvas renderer.

## Extensions

The following extension dialects are used in this document.
Each extension is defined in the Appendix or resolved via its URI.

| Term        | URI                            |
|-------------|--------------------------------|
| `type`      | `org.dxos.mdl.type@1.0`       |
| `feat`      | `org.dxos.mdl.feat@1.0`       |
| `scenario`  | `org.dxos.mdl.scenario@1.0`   |
| `component` | `org.dxos.mdl.component@1.0`  |
| `op`        | `org.dxos.mdl.op@1.1`         |
| `service`   | `org.dxos.mdl.service@1.0`    |
| `test`      | `org.dxos.mdl.test@1.0`       |
| `step`      | `org.dxos.mdl.step@1.0`       |

## Types

```mdl
type ClassNode
  desc: A canvas node of type `class`; stored in a NodeRecord like any canvas node.
  fields:
    name: string
    attributes: string[]
    methods: string[]
```

## Components

```mdl
component UmlSkill
  desc: UML class diagrams from source code (bound documents or a fetched GitHub reference):
        the agent extracts the class model, emits a mermaid classDiagram, and plugin-illustrator's
        generate operation compiles and lays it out.

component ClassNodeView
  desc: The class shape: a name compartment over attribute and method compartments, each edited in place.
```

## Features

```mdl
feat F-1: Class shape on the canvas

  req F-1.1: With plugin-canvas enabled, the canvas palette offers a Class tool.
  req F-1.2:
    when: a class is created
    then: it shows a name, one attribute and one method as placeholders
  req F-1.3:
    when: a compartment is double-clicked
    then: it edits in place; attributes and methods are one per line
  req F-1.4: The properties panel edits name, attributes and methods.
```

```mdl
feat F-2: Inheritance arrow

  req F-2.1: A link's end marker may be a hollow triangle (UML generalization).
```

```mdl
feat F-3: UML skill

  req F-3.1: The UML skill is registered while the plugin is enabled, and absent when it is not.
```

## QA

```mdl
test QA-1: Draw a class and an inheritance link on the canvas
  desc: The class shape's round-trip on the canvas — create, edit in place, link with an inheritance arrow.
  actors: human
  covers: [F-1.1, F-1.2, F-1.3, F-2.1]
  status: unverified
  given:
    - an identity exists
    - space: a space is open
    - collection: a collection in that space, to create into
    - plugin-canvas and plugin-uml are enabled
    - no drawing named "QA UML Canvas" exists — ABORT rather than deleting one this test did not create
  steps:
    - name: Create a canvas drawing
      do: In the navtree, click + on the collection, choose Drawing, pick the Canvas renderer and name it "QA UML Canvas".
      expect: an empty canvas opens with the palette on the left, including a Class tool
    - name: Draw two classes
      do: Pick the Class tool and drag out a box; repeat for a second box beside it.
      expect: each box shows "Class", "id: string" and "save(): void" in three compartments
    - name: Rename a class
      do: Double-click the first class's name, type "Person" and press Enter.
      expect: the first class's name compartment reads "Person"
    - name: Link with inheritance
      do: Drag from the second class to the first with the Smart line tool; select the link and set its End to Triangle.
      expect: the link ends at "Person" in a hollow triangle
  after:
    - name: Delete the drawing
      do: Right-click "QA UML Canvas" in the navtree and choose Delete.
      expect: the row leaves the navtree and its plank closes
```

## Appendix: Extension Definitions

Extension block types used in this document are defined below using
the core `ext` primitive — the only construct the base language provides.

```mdl
ext type
  uri: org.dxos.mdl.type@1.0
  desc: A named data structure with typed fields and optional literals.
  fields:
    desc?: Prose
    fields?: FieldMap        # name[?]: TypeExpr  (# inline comment)
    literals?: UnionList     # a | b | c
    extends?: TypeRef[]
```

```mdl
ext feat
  uri: org.dxos.mdl.feat@1.0
  desc: A named feature grouping one or more requirements.
  fields:
    desc?: Prose
    req: RequirementList
  nesting: self              # feat blocks may contain feat blocks
```

```mdl
ext scenario
  uri: org.dxos.mdl.scenario@1.0
  desc: An acceptance scenario expressed as given / when / then steps.
  fields:
    given?: Step | Step[]
    when?: Step | Step[]
    then: Step | Step[]
    tags?: TagList
```

```mdl
ext component
  uri: org.dxos.mdl.component@1.0
  desc: A UI component with props, internal state, slots, actions, and events.
  fields:
    desc?: Prose
    props?: FieldMap            # external inputs (immutable inside component)
    state?: FieldMap            # internal reactive state
    slots?: FieldMap            # named ReactNode injection points
    actions?: ActionMap         # methods the component exposes or handles
    emits?: EventMap            # events the component raises to its parent
    layout?: CodeBlock          # ASCII sketch of visual structure (non-normative)
```

```mdl
ext op
  uri: org.dxos.mdl.op@1.0
  desc: |
    A named operation with typed inputs, outputs, and declared errors.
    Pure ops have no effects or requires. Effectful ops declare both.
  fields:
    desc?: Prose
    input?: FieldMap            # named input parameters
    output?: TypeExpr           # return type
    errors?: ErrorMap           # name: Prose  (when this error occurs)
    effects?: EffectList        # echo:read | echo:write | http | fs | ...
    requires?: ServiceList      # injected service dependencies
    note?: Prose                # implementation guidance (non-normative)
```

```mdl
ext service
  uri: org.dxos.mdl.service@1.0
  desc: An external or system-level dependency providing named operations.
  fields:
    desc?: Prose
    loading?: eager | lazy
    ops?: OpMap                 # name(params) → ReturnType
    errors?: ErrorMap
    note?: Prose
```
